# Custom domain & SSL safety (docs.t3planet.de)

Production URL: https://docs.t3planet.de/en/latest

## Incident lesson (2026-09-25)

Deleting/recreating the Cloudflare custom hostname for `docs.t3planet.de` to “flush cache” **removed the live SSL certificate**. The site then failed with `ERR_SSL_VERSION_OR_CIPHER_MISMATCH` until DNS ACME TXT was updated and validation completed.

**Do not repeat that mistake.**

## Absolute prohibitions

Never do any of the following as a cache, CDN, or “stuck page” fix:

1. `deployment.deleteCustomHostname` / delete custom hostname
2. `deployment.removeCustomDomain` / remove `docs.t3planet.de`
3. Delete + recreate custom hostname “to flush edge cache”
4. Change `_acme-challenge.docs` / `_cf-custom-hostname.docs` DNS without an approved SSL recovery plan
5. Change `docs` CNAME away from `cname.mintlify.builders` without operator approval
6. Clear, rewrite, or rotate SSL/DCV records “just in case”

## Allowed cache / stale-content actions

Use only safe paths:

1. Confirm origin first: `https://t3planet.mintlify.app/en/latest/...` (or `.mintlify.site`)
2. Wait for Mintlify deploy to finish; re-check live HTML content markers
3. Hard refresh / private window / cache-bust query on the URL
4. Local LAN purge only: `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:3000/__t3_cache_purge`
5. Content fix: edit `.md` / redirects / `.mintignore` → commit as **Nitsan** → push org `master` → wait for deploy

If custom domain looks stale but origin is correct: **wait and re-test**. Report edge lag. Do **not** touch hostname/SSL.

## If SSL is already broken (recovery only)

1. STOP destructive hostname churn.
2. Read current required records via Mintlify (`getCustomHostnameStatus`).
3. Ask the operator to update **All-Inkl / Kasserver** DNS to the **exact** current TXT/CNAME values (or preferred DCV CNAME).
4. Retrigger validation only after DNS matches on authoritative NS (`ns5`/`ns6.kasserver.com`).
5. Do not claim live fixed until `https://docs.t3planet.de/en/latest` returns 200 with a valid cert.

Hostname delete/recreate for recovery requires **explicit operator authorization** and a ready DNS update in the same change window.

